        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Support intake and validation\nThis section receives the support request from the webhook, extracts the request body into a clean structure, and confirms that key values like customer email and message are present before any AI processing begins. It helps ensure the workflow only continues with valid support submissions"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6991c541-c44b-49e1-bf9e-91ad39651ed0",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -848,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 464,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Priority calculation and escalation check\n\nThis section converts the AI priority result into your internal support priority format, prepares ticket naming and timestamps, and checks whether the case is urgent enough to require escalation handling. It creates a consistent operational layer between AI output and your actual support process.\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c5338294-0251-4d33-a676-9ee33406c805",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -336,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 464,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Ticket creation and payload preparation\n\nThis section creates the Jira support ticket using the customer message and AI triage details, then builds one final combined payload containing original request data, AI insights, ticket details, and routing fields. It gives all later nodes one clean object to work with."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "62e09661-9071-4d31-a003-af39dae95229",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1504,
        16
