    {
      "id": "6bbdec0d-3b8c-4479-8104-e8ac0e3c4f0c",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3040,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 784,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "# AI Support Triage with Gemini Jira Slack Gmail Webhook\n## How it works:\nThis workflow receives support requests via webhook, validates customer data, and uses Google Gemini AI to classify issues into billing, technical, or general categories with priority assessment. AI responses are parsed into structured JSON, converted to P1-P4 priorities, and used to create Jira tickets. Notifications route to correct support teams via Slack channels and Gmail emails with priority, customer details, and contact information for immediate action.\n## Setup Steps:\n1. Webhook Intake Configure Incoming Support Webhook for POST requests on support-triage path.\n2. Data Normalization and Validation Normalize webhook payload and validate required fields like message and customer_email.\n3. AI Classification and Parsing Google Gemini AI agent classifies issues and parses response into structured JSON.\n4. Priority Mapping Convert AI labels to P1-P4 priorities and detect urgent escalation cases.\n5. Jira Ticket Creation Generate Jira support ticket in project 10000 with full customer and AI analysis details.\n6. Team Routing and Notifications Route to billing/technical/general teams via Switch node, then send Slack channel alerts and Gmail team emails."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
